<p><strong>A beauty, skin or aesthetic clinic in Nepal needs software that schedules the practitioner and the treatment room together, sells courses of treatments, records deposits and payments, and gives the owner one clear report. It is a scheduling and payment tool, not a medical records system.</strong></p>
<p>Clinic treatments are longer than a haircut, they need specific rooms or equipment, and many clients buy a course. Booking by phone and a paper file makes all three harder than they need to be.</p>
<h2>Practitioner and room scheduling</h2>
<p>Each treatment needs a named practitioner and a free room for the whole session. Software should stop a room or practitioner being booked twice and let reception see the day at a glance. See <a href="/features/booking/">how Zennly books</a>.</p>
<h2>Courses and packages</h2>
<p>Many treatments are sold as a course. Track what the client bought, redeem each visit and show how many sessions remain. Read about <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a>.</p>
<h2>Deposits and payments</h2>
<p>Record deposits, balances and the payment method against each booking, so the daily close matches the till. See <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a>.</p>
<h2>Controls for the owner</h2>
<p>Staff discounts and refunds should be approved and recorded, and different roles should see different things. See <a href="/features/discount-management/">discount management</a> and <a href="/features/role-based-access/">role-based access</a>.</p>
